      "title": "POSITION OVERVIEW",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Southwestern University Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Gifts and Grants Accountant | Southwestern University Careers page has loaded. Gifts and Grants Accountant | Southwestern University Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Southwestern University Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Gifts and Grants Accountant Print Apply ﻿ Gifts and Grants Accountant Location Georgetown, Texas 78626 Job Type Staff - Full Time, Exempt, Regular Job Number 202600096 Division Finance & Administration Department Finance and Administration Opening Date 08/31/2026 Description Benefits ABOUT US Located in Georgetown, Texas, Southwestern University is an independent, four-year undergraduate institution offers a top-ranked integrated arts and sciences curriculum that incorporates the humanities, fine arts, social sciences, and natural sciences. At Southwestern University, we are committed to fostering an environment where every individual feels respected, valued, and empowered. We believe that a thriving community is built on the strength of varying perspectives and experiences, and we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect and understanding. Our actions are guided by a commitment to fairness, openness, and the belief that our differences are what make us stronger as a whole. POSITION OVERVIEW Reporting to the Associate Vice President of Budgeting & Planning, the Gifts and Grants Accountant is responsible for the administration and oversight of the University’s operating, grant, restricted, and agency fund accounts, including monthly account reconciliations. This position exercises independent judgment and discretion while working collaboratively with budget officers and campus partners to support effective financial management and compliance with University policies and procedures. Key responsibilities include reviewing and approving requests to fill positions, purchase requisitions, procurement card transactions, and contracts. The Gifts and Grants Accountant also serves as the primary administrator for general ledger (GL) account setup and provides appropriate access to business functions within the University’s ERP system and other business platforms. Additional responsibilities include journal entries, supporting fiscal year-end closeout activities, assisting with audits, and performing other accounting and financial functions on a daily, monthly, and annual basis. DUTIES Responsible for overseeing and administration of designated operating accounts (fund 11, 12 & 14), all grants (fund 22), restricted funds (fund 21) and agency (fund 71) including independently working with the appropriate budget officers, setting up and monitoring grant budgets, reviewing expenses, and ensuring compliance with federal and grant requirements, and all related financial reporting and invoicing. Oversees expenses to ensure the funds are used for allowed purposes and provides final approval before payment. Provide new account numbers, monitor budgets, and communicate with budget officers. Independently gathers necessary information and prepares monthly operational journal entries to properly account for Southwestern operations, including physical plant charge outs, utility allocations, indirect salary allocations, postage and other monthly charges as assigned. Provide general professional accounting support within the Business Office involving compilation, consolidation, and analysis of financial data (i.e. ledgers, preparing journal entries, compliance with internal controls, reconciliations, etc.) especially as it relates to month-end and year-end tasks by established deadlines. Serves as Business Office main contact for theatre box office, which includes reviewing box office deposits and analyzing monthly reports for accuracy. Prepares monthly invoices and related journal entries & performs necessary collections related to third-party external organizations that owe Southwestern University. Primary contact for indirect cost rate (IDC) for the University including preparing data analysis and collection during the IDC renewal cycles. Prepares annual NSF HERD survey and other surveys as required by granting agency or as assigned. Review and maintain the general ledger user defined fields of the trial balance. Additional Duties: Support audit work paper preparation. Support budget preparation and review. Assist with special accounting projects. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or related field. Three years professional-level experience in accounting or project accounting. Possess strong accounting and data analysis skills and astute problem-solving ability. Demonstrate strong understanding in budgeting, project accounting and financial record keeping. Demonstrate advanced excel and word processing software skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Demonstrated leadership skills, including a strong work ethic. Excellent organizational skills and the ability to handle multiple tasks with a keen attention to detail. Possess excellent interaction and communication skills (verbal and written). Have knowledge, understanding, and acceptance of cultural differences and the diversity within the campus and community. Demonstrated professional manner with all internal and external University constituencies. Ability to be flexible, adjust to fluctuating priorities, perform well in stressful situations, and produce a reliable work product. Possess the applications of tact, diplomacy, sensitivity, and confidentiality. Understanding and commitment to a liberal arts education, including the ability to relate to a liberal arts faculty. Ability to attend work consistently and maintain a regular work schedule. Preferred Position Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or Business. Five + years of professional-level accounting experience, with demonstrated knowledge of project accounting and federal grant compliance. Prior experience using Datatel, Cashnet/Transact, Concur and Softdocs. Work experience in higher education or non-profit organization. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Starting annual salary: $62,826. The final offer for the successful candidate will be commensurate with experience and may exceed the starting annual salary. This position is not eligible for employer immigration sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without requiring employer-sponsored work authorization. All individuals hired are required to complete the federal employment eligibility verification process as required by applicable law. Southwestern University is an E-Verify employer. Southwestern University is an equal-opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. We do not discriminate in hiring on the basis of sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please contact us by email at hr@southwestern.edu. Jeanne Clery Statement: Notice of Availability of Annual Security and Fire Safety Report— Southwestern University Annual Safety and Fire Report is available online at https://www.southwestern.edu/life-at-southwestern/safety-security/annual-security-reports/ containing mandated information about current campus policies concerning safety and security issues, required statistics, and other related information for the past three calendar years. To obtain a paper copy of the report, please call 512-863-1435. Southwestern University offers a comprehensive benefits package, which includes health and welfare insurance (medical, dental, and vision), life and AD&D insurance, long-term disability coverage, generous contributions to a 403(b) retirement account, an Employee Assistance Program (EAP), various paid time-off programs (for staff positions), undergraduate tuition assistance for you and your dependents, access to athletic facilities, free parking, and discounted meal rates, along with other benefits designed to support your well-being and work-life balance. Employer Southwestern University Address 1001 E University Ave Georgetown, Texas, 78626 Phone 5128631435 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternati